steps.text:
`OutlinedInput` already supports auto-sizing textareas. Don’t pass `TextareaAutosize` as `inputComponent`; use `multiline` instead:

```jsx
<OutlinedInput
  multiline
  rowsMin={3}
  rowsMax={8}
/>
```

In Material-UI v4.11, custom `inputComponent`s are given an `inputRef` prop. `TextareaAutosize` expects its ref via React’s normal `ref`, so it forwards `inputRef` to the native `<textarea>`, causing the warning.

If a custom component is required, adapt the ref:

```jsx
const AutosizeInput = React.forwardRef(function AutosizeInput(props, ref) {
  const { inputRef, ...other } = props;
  return <TextareaAutosize {...other} ref={inputRef || ref} />;
});

<OutlinedInput inputComponent={AutosizeInput} />
```

But `multiline` is the intended and simpler solution.
